  "summary_en": "Industry association BSA's submission to Brazil's MCTIC consultation on its National AI Strategy. It opposes one-size-fits-all AI regulation, urges updating existing laws (including a text-and-data-mining copyright exception), proposes software security as a core principle, and supports open government data, workforce development and cross-border data flows.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Avoid one-size-fits-all AI regulation; modernize existing frameworks and use tailored responses",
   "Amend Brazilian Copyright Law to add a text and data mining exception",
   "Include software security as a core principle of the Strategy",
   "Clarify roles and responsibilities of stakeholders across the AI value chain, per OECD principles",
   "Support open government data, workforce development and cross-border data flow rules in trade agreements"
  ],
